/**
 * Scene for "A record with fields" (lesson c/concepto-de-estructuras, order: 22), a
 * short film played on one persistent motion canvas. The captions and cues live in
 * `src/data/animations/estructuras-registros-c.ts`.
 *
 * The canvas has two halves. The editor on the left is a fixed overlay: four of the
 * lesson's programs take turns in it, with a bar that slides to the running line and
 * the real output typed in the console below. The viewport on the right holds the
 * camera: an isometric world with four stations. A `struct` is a plate whose fields
 * are cells laid out one after another (name on the front edge, value on top); an
 * array is a column of plates; calling a function copies the whole plate into a frame
 * raised above `main`; an `enum` is a shelf of named integers; a `union` is a single
 * cell with two names; and padding shows on byte strips, where gaps are magenta.
 * Every instruction is a module labelled with its editor line. One visual identity
 * per concept: light blue for the flow and for plain data, violet for what resolves
 * a problem (the tag, the returned copy), magenta for what is lost or wasted.
 *
 * Palette: films are the approved exception to the Organic palette (DESIGN.md §8).
 * The colors are the `--xj-*` tokens declared once in the style block; nothing
 * else in the file uses a raw color.
 */
